12375	{"artifactId":"LLD-c32aa60534232f36-s7","entry":{"id":"review-65ce97e1ccfd5b8c1d6ef084173eec15","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-30T13:54:03.385Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each of EXT-c32aa60534232f36-s7's acceptance criteria (ac1-ac7) is designed in the LLD and mapped to a proving test in §7's Acceptance mapping table, with no non-goal (sibling-owned scope) implemented.","evidence":"EXT.md lists ac1..ac7 verbatim; LLD §7 Acceptance mapping has one row per ac1-ac7, each pointing to concrete test subjects also enumerated in the Test levels; §1 'Adjacent scope' explicitly excludes s1-s6 owned work and §5 states S7 'does not implement a replacement shared contract, state machine, evidence ledger, recovery store or publisher.'","action":"Read EXT.md and cross-referenced the ac list against LLD §7's table and §1's adjacent-scope exclusions.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design's claim that 'Default remains legacy' / the default engine today is legacy is true of the running code.","evidence":"src/daemon/review-investigation-adoption.ts readInvestigationSelection(): `engine:raw.codeReview?.engine??'legacy'` — falls back to 'legacy' whenever codeReview.engine is unset. [files: src/daemon/review-investigation-adoption.ts]","action":"Read readInvestigationSelection() in review-investigation-adoption.ts.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design's description of today's scope-selection mechanism ('Existing separately approved ISSUE scope references remain readable'; trailers alone cannot establish exclusive ownership) matches the real CanonicalReviewWorkAdapter.readAttestation implementation.","evidence":"src/daemon/review-investigation-work.ts readAttestation() requires a `scope:ISSUE-...@rev#digest` reference resolved against an approved ISSUE's `fixIntent` (`kind:'review-scope-v1'`) and explicitly throws 'Explicit approved scope reference is required; commit trailers are insufficient' when no such reference is supplied. [files: src/daemon/review-investigation-work.ts]","action":"Read CanonicalReviewWorkAdapter.readAttestation in review-investigation-work.ts.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"scopedReviewToolCatalog, createScopedReviewMcpServer and runNativeInvestigationSession, described in §2.1-2.3 as existing functions gaining a new optional `protocol` parameter, already exist today with matching core signatures and the stated backward-compatible shape (old callers calling with the current single/triple-arg form are unaffected).","evidence":"src/shared/review-investigation-catalog.ts exports `scopedReviewToolCatalog(indexed:boolean)`; src/mcp/review-investigation-bridge.ts exports `createScopedReviewMcpServer(binding,indexed,forward)`; src/agent/providers/native-investigation-session.ts exports `runNativeInvestigationSession(input:NativeInvestigationInvocation):Promise<InvestigationReplyV1>` — identical return type and base parameters to the LLD's contract. [files: src/shared/review-investigation-catalog.ts, src/mcp/review-investigation-bridge.ts, src/agent/providers/native-investigation-session.ts]","action":"Read all three source files and compared exported signatures against LLD §2.1-2.3.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"InvestigationRepository and InvestigationAdoptionPolicy, described in §2.4-2.5 as existing classes with the given method shapes, already exist with matching methods (start/advance/view/cancel; assertSelected/evidence/adapter).","evidence":"src/daemon/review-investigation-repository.ts defines `class InvestigationRepository` with `start`, `advance`, `view`, `cancel`, `complete` methods; src/daemon/review-investigation-adoption.ts defines `class InvestigationAdoptionPolicy` with `assertSelected()`, `async evidence(mode)`, `async adapter(repo,mode)` matching the LLD interface almost verbatim (the real `advance` takes one additional optional `receivedCommand` param the LLD omits, which is additive and not a contradiction). [files: src/daemon/review-investigation-repository.ts, src/daemon/review-investigation-adoption.ts]","action":"Read both classes in full and diffed method signatures against LLD §2.4-2.5.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"All files listed as 'Call sites' for the new compact-protocol data model item (§3.1) exist and already contain the related existing exports the compact protocol is meant to extend.","evidence":"src/shared/review-investigation-catalog.ts, src/mcp/review-investigation-bridge.ts, src/mcp/review-investigation-native.ts and src/agent/providers/native-investigation-session.ts all exist and already import/export scopedReviewToolCatalog / createScopedReviewMcpServer / startNativeReviewBroker / runNativeInvestigationSession as the LLD assumes. [files: src/shared/review-investigation-catalog.ts, src/mcp/review-investigation-bridge.ts, src/mcp/review-investigation-native.ts, src/agent/providers/native-investigation-session.ts]","action":"Read each file and confirmed the named exports/imports are present.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The call sites named for the new 'Canonical BUILD review scope and TESTS metadata' field-add (§3.3) — src/daemon/review-investigation-work.ts, src/daemon/review-investigation-repository.ts, src/workflow/runners/build/test-record.ts, src/workflow/runners/build/round-writer.ts — all exist, and the inventory correctly does not yet contain a `reviewScope` field (consistent with this being new, not already-built, work).","evidence":"grep for `reviewScope` across the repo returns no matches outside the LLD/artifact files themselves, confirming the field truly does not exist yet; all four named files exist (confirmed by Glob of src/workflow/runners/build/*.ts and reading review-investigation-work.ts). [files: src/daemon/review-investigation-work.ts, src/workflow/runners/build/test-record.ts, src/workflow/runners/build/round-writer.ts]","action":"Grepped for `reviewScope` repo-wide and globbed src/workflow/runners/build/*.ts.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"§3.3's claim that 'old test evidence remains unknown when it cannot be bound to the reviewed source' has a concrete, specified data shape for that 'unknown' state in the existing TESTS metadata model, so builders know what to persist.","evidence":"src/workflow/runners/build/test-record.ts defines `TestCaseResult = 'pass' | 'fail' | 'skipped' | 'not found'` and `TestRecordFile.titles[].result: 'pass'|'fail'|'skipped'` — there is no 'unknown'/'unbound' value in either union today, and LLD §3's only schemaDiff snippet covers the compact native-protocol types (ReviewModelProtocol/CompactFinalAck/ReviewToolError), not any TestRecord/TESTS schema change. The design states the behavior but never specifies the new type/field needed to represent it. [files: src/workflow/runners/build/test-record.ts]","action":"Read test-record.ts's type definitions and compared against LLD §3's schemaDiff, which omits any TestRecord-related type change.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.2","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The data-compatibility claim that BUILD/TESTS writes 'preserve canonical repo identity and history' and that abbreviated Git IDs are 'uniquely resolved and audited as the same object' rests on an existing mechanism, not an invented one.","evidence":"test-record.ts's `TestRecordTask.commit` is an optional pinned commit string rendered into TESTS.md ('Run at ... on commit `${task.commit}`'), consistent with existing per-run commit binding that the new scope work extends rather than replaces. [files: src/workflow/runners/build/test-record.ts]","action":"Read the TestRecordTask type and its markdown rendering in test-record.ts.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"sc7 (the MCP/daemon/controller start/status/resume/cancel transport) remains S6-owned in the HLD, and S7's consumption of it (rather than redesigning it) is backed by an already-approved local-consumer HLD amendment, matching §1's adjacent-scope note and §2.4's precondition.","evidence":"HLD.md line ~320 states sc7 is the 'Sole transport owner for plan-investigation-v1 code reviews' owned by s6; AMD-c32aa60534232f36-2.json records `amendment.type:'storyBoundary.addStory', storyId:'s7'` with `lifecycle.status:'approved'` (approval timestamp 2026-10-30T13:23:51Z) — i.e. the consumer declaration the LLD's precondition 2.4 calls for is already in place, not merely proposed. [files: docs/epics/review-planned-changes-through-agent-investigation-E20261028c32aa605/HLD.md, .insrc/artifacts/AMD-c32aa60534232f36-2.json]","action":"Read the HLD's sc7 ownership section and the AMD-2 amendment artifact's lifecycle status.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"§6's 'Finish requested with unresolved obligations' error path — that an incomplete finish surfaces unresolved rows/blocks rather than a false success — is grounded in an existing completion-assessment mechanism the new /tmp-report behavior would wrap, not a fabricated one.","evidence":"src/workflow/code-review/investigation/completion-assessment.ts's `assessReviewCompletion` already returns outcome `'incomplete'` with concrete `reasons` and `unresolvedRows` (pending/unverified coverage rows, blocks without a final 'reviewed' disposition, open outstanding work, unsettled attempts) whenever completion criteria are not met — exactly the accepted-state data the LLD's new inconclusive /tmp report is specified to be 'derived only from'. [files: src/workflow/code-review/investigation/completion-assessment.ts]","action":"Read assessReviewCompletion in full and matched its `incomplete` branch against the LLD's error-path description.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The integration-level test files the LLD names as already-existing suites to extend (review-investigation-recovery.test.ts, review-investigation-adoption.test.ts, test-record.test.ts, test-record-revision.test.ts) exist in the repo.","evidence":"Glob confirmed src/daemon/__tests__/review-investigation-recovery.test.ts, src/daemon/__tests__/review-investigation-adoption.test.ts, src/workflow/runners/build/__tests__/test-record.test.ts and test-record-revision.test.ts all exist. [files: src/daemon/__tests__/review-investigation-recovery.test.ts, src/daemon/__tests__/review-investigation-adoption.test.ts, src/workflow/runners/build/__tests__/test-record.test.ts, src/workflow/runners/build/__tests__/test-record-revision.test.ts]","action":"Glob + file-match search for these filenames.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":1,"low":11,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-30T13:54:03.385Z","model":"cli-claude:claude-sonnet-5","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
